# CODEOWNERS — real ownership, from .team/org.md
#
# Replaces a placeholder that mapped everything to `@xoroh/kern` and whose own
# comment admitted: "Rename to your real maintainer team/user (or delete this
# file) before enforcing code-owner reviews."
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS: `disclosure.test.tsx > Autocomplete > suggests matches while
# typing` had no recoverable owner. `git log` traced it to `b84a96c`, authored as
# `Xoroh <kern@xoroh.org>` — a bulk system commit with no per-agent authorship —
# and CODEOWNERS pointed at a single team. The cost was a dispatch spent
# diagnosing an ownerless test. That is the recurring cost this file removes.
#
# THE OLD RULES WERE ALSO STALE. Three of its five entries named files that no
# longer exist:
#   packages/mcp/src/component-sources.ts  deleted in 24f7810
#   packages/kern/src/theme/tokens.css     moved to packages/kern-tokens/ (D-034)
# A rule for a file that is gone is a rule that never fires — which is how a file
# accreted ownership rules that silently stopped describing anything.
#
# ORDER MATTERS. CODEOWNERS is last-match-wins, so specific rules come AFTER the
# broad `*`. Read bottom-up for the effective owner of any path.
#
# A path whose owner is genuinely ambiguous is listed under AMBIGUOUS and
# deliberately NOT given a rule. A wrong CODEOWNERS routes reviews to the wrong
# lane with the authority of a config file; an absent one routes them to everyone,
# which is merely slower.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- default lane
*                                       @xoroh/kern

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- web app
apps/site/                              @xoroh/site-se

# --------------------------------------------------------- tokens + elevation
# design-system-lead owns the token source of truth, the generated CSS, the
# theme spec, and the MCP manifest generation that reads them.
packages/kern-tokens/                  @xoroh/design-system-lead
packages/mcp/scripts/generate-manifest.mjs @xoroh/design-system-lead
packages/mcp/scripts/generate-maturity.mjs @xoroh/design-system-lead

# --------------------------------------------------------- kernel + primitives
# The design language lives in kern-native alongside kern-lead, so both are named
# there: a change to a native token binding is not kern-lead's alone.
packages/kern/                         @xoroh/kern-lead
packages/kern-native/                  @xoroh/kern-lead @xoroh/design-system-lead
packages/kern-primitives/              @xoroh/kern-lead @xoroh/design-system-lead

# ------------------------------------------------------------- gates (kern-lead)
# design-system-lead is on the boundary and layer gates because they police the
# package graph it maintains.
scripts/check-consumption.mjs          @xoroh/kern-lead
scripts/check-pack.mjs                 @xoroh/kern-lead
scripts/check-workflow.mjs             @xoroh/kern-lead
scripts/check-currency.mjs             @xoroh/kern-lead
scripts/check-parity.mjs               @xoroh/kern-lead @xoroh/design-system-lead
scripts/check-primitives.mjs           @xoroh/kern-lead @xoroh/design-system-lead
scripts/check-layers.mjs               @xoroh/kern-lead @xoroh/design-system-lead

# -------------------------------------------------------------- build tooling
# librarian owns build config, tsconfig, biome, module boundaries, and this file.
biome.json                             @xoroh/librarian
package.json                           @xoroh/librarian
packages/*/tsconfig.json                @xoroh/librarian
.githooks/                             @xoroh/librarian
.github/workflows/                    @xoroh/librarian
.github/CODEOWNERS                     @xoroh/librarian

# ------------------------------------------- SHARED — review-all, do not assume
# Touched by several lanes, so a reviewer is routed to MORE than one rather than
# to whichever lane happened to edit last.
parity/contract.ts                     @xoroh/kern-lead @xoroh/design-system-lead

# ------------------------------------------------------ generated — generator owns
# Editing these by hand is the defect the freshness gate exists to catch, so the
# owner is whoever can re-run the generator.
packages/mcp/src/manifest.ts           @xoroh/design-system-lead
packages/mcp/src/maturity.ts           @xoroh/design-system-lead
docs/components.md                     @xoroh/design-system-lead
docs/elevation-audit.md                @xoroh/design-system-lead

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- AMBIGUOUS
# Deliberately UNOWNED — no rule above, so these fall through to `*`
# (@xoroh/kern). Each is a real gap, listed rather than guessed:
#
#   packages/kern-icons/assets/sets/   drop-in icon sets. No lane has claimed
#                                      the corpus and no set ships yet, so a rule
#                                      would assert ownership of nothing.
#   packages/kern-icons/src/sets/      the generated default set. Which lane owns
#                                      GENERATING it is not established.
#   .changeset/                         release notes. Written by whoever lands
#                                      the change, so a static owner is wrong.
#   packages/cli/                       no lane has claimed it.
#
# Each needs a ruling. Until then `@xoroh/kern` is the safe default rather than a
# false attribution.